From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Thibaud Michaud <thibaudm@chromium.org>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 16:57:31 +0100
Subject: [regalloc] Fix off-by-one deferred-region clamp in AllocateBlockedReg

In LinearScanAllocator::AllocateBlockedReg, when clamping `new_end` to
the end of the current deferred region in a deferred block,
`GapFromInstructionIndex(LastDeferredInstructionIndex(block))` computed
the start of the last deferred instruction (4*L) rather than the end of
the deferred region after that instruction (4*(L + 1)).

When a live range started at or inside the last instruction of a
deferred block (positions [4*L, 4*L + 3]), clamping `new_end` to 4*L
produced `new_end <= current->Start()`, preventing the range from
stealing an available register for the last deferred instruction or
triggering a degenerate split when `current->Start() > 4*L`.

Use `InstructionFromInstructionIndex(...).NextFullStart()` to clamp to
the end boundary of the deferred region, matching `next_block_boundary`
in `AllocateRegisters`.

Bug: 560620348
Change-Id: If367a86d127246a7c54ae3db1f366cd7811ce358
Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/v8/v8/+/8742800
Reviewed-by: Daniel Lehmann <dlehmann@chromium.org>
Commit-Queue: Thibaud Michaud <thibaudm@chromium.org>
Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#111714}

Electron adaptation notes (43-x-y): On this branch AllocateBlockedReg guards the clamp with `spill_mode == SpillMode::kSpillDeferred` and names the block `deferred_block` (main uses `block->IsDeferred()`); the condition is kept as-is and only the new_end computation is changed to InstructionFromInstructionIndex(...).NextFullStart() as upstream.

diff --git a/src/compiler/backend/register-allocator.cc b/src/compiler/backend/register-allocator.cc
index 3778c0377b40be192d7147d25a32bdda2010db97..402b5c1daed5d35231b2ebd8f03d055d8716e88a 100644
--- a/src/compiler/backend/register-allocator.cc
+++ b/src/compiler/backend/register-allocator.cc
@@ -4374,8 +4374,9 @@ void LinearScanAllocator::AllocateBlockedReg(LiveRange* current,
     InstructionBlock* deferred_block =
         code()->GetInstructionBlock(current->Start().ToInstructionIndex());
     new_end =
-        std::min(new_end, LifetimePosition::GapFromInstructionIndex(
-                              LastDeferredInstructionIndex(deferred_block)));
+        std::min(new_end, LifetimePosition::InstructionFromInstructionIndex(
+                              LastDeferredInstructionIndex(deferred_block))
+                              .NextFullStart());
   }
 
   // We couldn't spill until the next register use. Split before the register
diff --git a/test/unittests/compiler/regalloc/register-allocator-unittest.cc b/test/unittests/compiler/regalloc/register-allocator-unittest.cc
index cf14b5d96f6e0baa7eccdedd7de19cc8354d33b8..4326b109b6ab665f9b920c2e8673ab7b9c32b208 100644
--- a/test/unittests/compiler/regalloc/register-allocator-unittest.cc
+++ b/test/unittests/compiler/regalloc/register-allocator-unittest.cc
@@ -788,6 +788,48 @@ INSTANTIATE_TEST_SUITE_P(
     ::testing::Combine(::testing::ValuesIn(kParameterTypes),
                        ::testing::Range(0, SlotConstraintTest::kMaxVariant)));
 
+TEST_F(RegisterAllocatorTest, AllocateBlockedRegDeferredClampBelowStart) {
+  SetNumRegs(3, 1);
+
+  // B0 (non-deferred): branch selector `c`, value `d` used at the deferred
+  // jump, and phi inputs `w0..w2` creating register pressure.
+  StartBlock();
+  VReg c = Parameter(Reg());
+  VReg d = Define(Reg());
+  VReg w0 = Define(Reg());
+  VReg w1 = Define(Reg());
+  VReg w2 = Define(Reg());
+  EndBlock(Branch(Reg(c), 1, 2));  // succs: B1 (deferred), B2
+
+  // B1 (deferred): a call clobbers all registers, defs re-occupy all
+  // registers, ending with a jump that uses `d` in a register. The next block
+  // in RPO order (B2) is not deferred.
+  StartBlock(true);
+  EmitCall(Slot(-1));
+  VReg z0 = Define(Reg());
+  VReg z1 = Define(Reg());
+  VReg z2 = Define(Reg());
+  EndBlock(Jump(2, Reg(d)));  // succ: B3
+
+  // B2 (non-deferred; predecessor B0).
+  StartBlock();
+  EmitNop();
+  EndBlock(Jump(1));  // succ: B3
+
+  // B3: merge with phis keeping `z0..z2` live out of B1, and a late use of `d`
+  // so that its split child survives past the B2 block boundary.
+  StartBlock();
+  VReg p0 = Phi(z0, w0);
+  VReg p1 = Phi(z1, w1);
+  VReg p2 = Phi(z2, w2);
+  EmitI(Use(d));
+  EmitI(Use(p0), Use(p1), Use(p2));
+  Return(p0);
+  EndBlock(Last());
+
+  Allocate();
+}
+
